setup.body:
Create /etc/claude-code/managed-settings.json (root, 0644) with the block below. If the file exists, add the two entries to its "hooks" instead of replacing it. Hooks in this file run for every user and cannot be turned off from a user's or a project's settings.

{
  "hooks": {
    "PreToolUse": [{"matcher": "*", "hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "/usr/local/lib/jt-ai-agent/jt-ai-agent-hook.py", "timeout": 5}]}],
    "SessionStart": [{"hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "/usr/local/lib/jt-ai-agent/jt-ai-agent-hook.py", "timeout": 5}]}]
  }
}

New sessions pick it up; running sessions may need a restart. For a single user only, the same block can go into that user's ~/.claude/settings.json (the user can remove it).

setup.body_zh:
建立 /etc/claude-code/managed-settings.json（root、0644），內容如下。檔案已經存在時，把這兩項加進它的 "hooks"，不要整份取代。這個檔案裡的 hook 對所有使用者生效，使用者或專案的設定都關不掉。

{
  "hooks": {
    "PreToolUse": [{"matcher": "*", "hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "/usr/local/lib/jt-ai-agent/jt-ai-agent-hook.py", "timeout": 5}]}],
    "SessionStart": [{"hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "/usr/local/lib/jt-ai-agent/jt-ai-agent-hook.py", "timeout": 5}]}]
  }
}

新的工作階段就會套用；執行中的工作階段可能要重新開始。只想對一個使用者啟用時，同一段可以放在該使用者的 ~/.claude/settings.json（他自己可以拿掉）。

setup.body:
1.2 adds four hook events to the same hook: PermissionRequest (the agent asks to be allowed a call), PostToolUseFailure for Claude Code (PostToolUse for Codex and opencode; the hook only writes a line when the call failed and never reads its output), SubagentStart and SessionEnd. Add them next to PreToolUse and SessionStart:
- Claude Code managed settings: "PermissionRequest" and "PostToolUseFailure" with "matcher": "*", "SubagentStart" and "SessionEnd" without a matcher, each running the same command;
- Codex /etc/codex/requirements.toml: [[hooks.PermissionRequest]] and [[hooks.PostToolUse]] with matcher ".*", [[hooks.SubagentStart]] and [[hooks.SessionEnd]], each running the hook with --agent codex;
- opencode: install the 1.2 plugin (it reports failed calls and permission requests itself).
On macOS the Claude Code file is /Library/Application Support/ClaudeCode/managed-settings.json and opencode's system plugins are in /Library/Application Support/opencode/plugins/; rotate the log with newsyslog (/etc/newsyslog.d/jt-ai-agent.conf: "/var/log/jt-ai-agent/actions.log 622 8 5000 * J"). The agent group has a Darwin block for the log and the file integrity of these paths.

The same hook, installed in each agent's system-wide configuration (root, 0644; merge into an existing file instead of replacing it). Each runs for every user on the host.

Gemini CLI: /etc/gemini-cli/settings.json (macOS: /Library/Application Support/GeminiCli/settings.json). System settings override user and project settings.
{
  "hooksConfig": {"enabled": true},
  "hooks": {
    "BeforeTool":   [{"matcher": "*", "hooks": [{"name": "jt-ai-agent", "type": "command", "command": "/usr/local/lib/jt-ai-agent/jt-ai-agent-hook.py --agent gemini", "timeout": 5000}]}],
    "AfterTool":    [{"matcher": "*", "hooks": [{"name": "jt-ai-agent", "type": "command", "command": "/usr/local/lib/jt-ai-agent/jt-ai-agent-hook.py --agent gemini", "timeout": 5000}]}],
    "SessionStart": [{"hooks": [{"name": "jt-ai-agent", "type": "command", "command": "/usr/local/lib/jt-ai-agent/jt-ai-agent-hook.py --agent gemini", "timeout": 5000}]}],
    "SessionEnd":   [{"hooks": [{"name": "jt-ai-agent", "type": "command", "command": "/usr/local/lib/jt-ai-agent/jt-ai-agent-hook.py --agent gemini", "timeout": 5000}]}],
    "Notification": [{"hooks": [{"name": "jt-ai-agent", "type": "command", "command": "/usr/local/lib/jt-ai-agent/jt-ai-agent-hook.py --agent gemini", "timeout": 5000}]}]
  }
}

Cursor: /etc/cursor/hooks.json (macOS: /Library/Application Support/Cursor/hooks.json). Only after-the-fact events: Cursor's before-hooks block a call when the answer is not what they expect.
{"version": 1, "hooks": {
  "sessionStart":       [{"command": "/usr/local/lib/jt-ai-agent/jt-ai-agent-hook.py --agent cursor", "timeout": 5}],
  "sessionEnd":         [{"command": "/usr/local/lib/jt-ai-agent/jt-ai-agent-hook.py --agent cursor", "timeout": 5}],
  "postToolUse":        [{"command": "/usr/local/lib/jt-ai-agent/jt-ai-agent-hook.py --agent cursor", "timeout": 5}],
  "postToolUseFailure": [{"command": "/usr/local/lib/jt-ai-agent/jt-ai-agent-hook.py --agent cursor", "timeout": 5}]
}}

GitHub Copilot (Copilot CLI; VS Code agent mode on the Copilot harness): /etc/github-copilot/policy.d/jt-ai-agent.json (same path on macOS). One entry per event, each passing its name; the trailing exit 0 matters, Copilot denies a preToolUse call when the hook fails.
{"version": 1, "hooks": {
  "preToolUse": [{"type": "command", "bash": "/usr/local/lib/jt-ai-agent/jt-ai-agent-hook.py --agent copilot --event preToolUse 2>/dev/null; exit 0", "timeoutSec": 5}],
  ... the same for sessionStart, sessionEnd, postToolUseFailure, subagentStart and permissionRequest
}}

Start new sessions afterwards (running ones keep their old configuration).
